    "summary": "Repaired the model and it now passes L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nRoot cause: the girder section instance had t_top = 0.20 m, while the description states the top slab is 0.18 m thick. The original girder.single.A/I decisions had been computed from the wrong 0.20 m top slab, so MR-02 recomputation from the corrected instance (t_top = 0.18 m) disagreed, failing L2-1. (There was no accepted-decision error in itself — the decisions were stale relative to the corrected geometry.)\n\nRepair actions:\n- Re-integrated the small-box middle-girder section from the described geometry (h=1.40, b_top=2.40, t_tip=0.18, haunch 0.201/0.062, b_bottom=1.00, t_bottom=0.18, t_top=0.18, t_web=0.20, web_slope 3.5, chamfers 0.15x0.07): A_single = 1.086349 m^2, I_single = 0.254757 m^4.\n- Revised girder.single.A/I and dependents: girder.A = 5.431747 m^2, girder.I = 1.273786 m^4, girder.w = 141.2254 kN/m, girder.m = 14.39566 t/m.\n- Re-ran the modal analysis: f1 = 4.2463 Hz; re-decided lane.mu = 0.23982 (JTG D60-2015 4.3.2).\n\nModel: single simply supported 25 m spine beam, 5 precast prestressed C40 small-box girders, 16 m deck, 4 design lanes, Class II, plain laminated elastomeric bearings (10 per abutment line) on both abutments, girder self-weight only.\n\nResults: vertical frequencies 4.246 / 16.797 / 37.065 Hz; self-weight support reactions 1765.3 kN each; self-weight midspan moment 11033.2 kN·m; lane max positive moment 6872.6 kN·m (no negative lane moment, simply supported)."
